   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to the\nresidency requirements for the persons performing the functions of building\ninspector/code enforcement officer and assistant/deputy building\ninspector/code enforcement officer for Putnam Valley, Putnam County",
    "basePrintNo": "S8928",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8928-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8928\n\nSPONSOR: SERINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the town law and the public officers\nlaw, in relation to the residency requirements for the persons perform-\ning the functions of building inspector/code enforcement officer and\nassistant/deputy building inspector/code enforcement officer for Putnam\nValley, Putnam County\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would exempt the residency requirement for building\ninspector/code enforcement officer or assistant/deputy building inspec-\ntor code enforcement officer in the town of Putnam Valley.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 explains that the town of Putnam Valley has employed individ-\nuals who reside outside of the town for positions that require town\nresidency. It validates, legalizes, ratifies, and confirms their employ-\nment of these individuals, notwithstanding the absence of prior legisla-\ntive approval.\n\nSection 2 amends Section 23 of the town law by adding a new subdivision\n32 to state that the positions of building inspector/code enforcement\nofficer and assistant/deputy building inspector code enforcement officer\ndo not need to be an elector of such town.\n\nSection 3 amends Section 3 of the public officers law by adding a new\nsubdivision 67 to state that the positions of building inspector/code\nenforcement officer and assistant/deputy building inspector code\nenforcement officer must be filled by a person who lives in Putnam Coun-\nty or any adjoining county.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder current law, the positions of building inspector/code enforcement\nofficer and assistant/deputy building inspector code enforcement officer\nin the Town of Putnam Valley must be filled by a resident of the Town of\nPutnam Valley. This bill will allow those positions to be filled by a\nresident of Putnam County or an adjourning county to Putnam County.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
